@meeting train.m19.calder
// SW3 (2026-10-26, Pillar 5 Step 5, S5-3): M19 Power and relays, Wednesday Day 17, 11:00, the relay room on Deck 1 (u).
// Calder; you swap a relay. If you have no conduit tester yet (M15 didn't give it), 24v plays her flag
// train.m19.tester after this. Then the relay rack's panel (m19.relay.*).
title: Power and relays
from: Chief Ines Calder
gist: Calder showed you the relay room: the bridge relays, how to find a slow one, and the battery banks on Deck 5. Your first Senior training.
== lines
calder > you: Your first Senior training. Fitting, up here. Everything on the bridge runs through this room.   [gesture]
calder: Twelve relays a rack. When one's slow, the bridge flickers. Then the bridge calls me.
calder: Watch the lights. Eleven come on together. One comes on late. That's your relay.
calder: Pull it straight. Seat the new one straight. Test the whole rack, not just the one.
? choice
* Why test the whole rack for one relay?   rel:calder+2
  calder: Because the slow one was hiding a second. It usually is.   [nod]
* (Just watch the lights)
  calder: Good. Patience with lights. Most people blink first.   [nod]
calder: Later, the batteries on Deck 5. Four banks. They have to share the load, like a good team.
calder: Your turn. The rack on the left. Take your time. I'm not timing you.
